					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Sourcing_Note" "Replaces the BAV199 that used to drop +BATT by a diode to make Vdrive. That trick existed only so 3.3V logic could clear the LEDs' V_IH, and the 5V boost on the ring board (U9 there) now does that job properly, so the drop is pure loss and Vdrive becomes +BATT. The bead is here rather than a 0R link because it works with C61 as an LC filter, keeping the ring boost's 1MHz switching current off +BATT, which also feeds the GNSS LNA and the LoRa module. Carries about 460mA worst case (5V/250mA out of the boost from a 3.0V cell), against a 1A rating; 150mOhm costs 70mV and 32mW there."
			(at 24.13 44.45 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
